# novadeck kernel config fragment — SUBTRACTIVE: non-Qualcomm platforms
#
# Merged after kernel.config by build.sh's `FRAGMENTS=("$KDIR_REPO"/*.config)` glob (the
# filename sorts after kernel.config, which is what we want: additions first, then cuts).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The build merges the mainline arm64 `defconfig` (build.sh, `merge_config.sh -m
# arch/arm64/configs/defconfig`), which is deliberately a "boots every arm64 board" config.
# kernel.config is purely ADDITIVE — it never emits a `# CONFIG_x is not set` — so before this
# file, every image shipped clocks, pinctrl, DRM, MMC, USB PHYs and DMA engines for ~47 SoC
# families that cannot exist on a soldered-SoC Qualcomm handheld. We boot SM8550/SM8650 only.
#
# METHOD: cut the PLATFORM GATES, not the drivers.
# Every entry below is a top-level platform gate from arch/arm64/Kconfig.platforms. Vendor
# drivers are gated on them (`depends on ARCH_TEGRA || COMPILE_TEST` and friends — ARCH_MXC
# alone is referenced in 148 Kconfig lines), so kconfig's dependency closure does the pruning.
# That is why this file is ~50 directives instead of ~1500, and why it MAINTAINS ITSELF: a
# vendor driver added upstream in a future kernel is born disabled, its gate already off.
#
# DO NOT convert this into a per-driver list. That is the version that rots.
#
# ##### SYNTAX TRAP — READ BEFORE EDITING #####
# merge_config.sh matches negative lines with `notset_regex = "^# CONFIG_[a-zA-Z0-9_]+ is not
# set$"` (scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh). That `$` is hard-anchored, so ANY trailing text
# turns the directive into an inert comment:
#
#     # CONFIG_ARCH_TEGRA is not set          # NVIDIA Tegra   <-- SILENTLY IGNORED
#     # CONFIG_ARCH_TEGRA is not set                           <-- correct
#
# It does not warn. The build succeeds and ships the drivers you thought you cut. That is why
# every description below sits on its OWN line above the directive, and why build.sh asserts
# this file actually took effect rather than trusting that it did (see the trim-platforms
# verification block there). Cost one wasted kernel build on 2026-08-03.
#
# Child SoC options cascade automatically and must NOT be listed here — ARCH_TEGRA_*_SOC,
# ARCH_R8A*/ARCH_RCAR_GEN*/ARCH_RZG2L (Renesas), and the umbrella symbols ARCH_BCM /
# ARCH_NXP / ARCH_MICROCHIP (select-ed by their children) all disappear on their own.
#
# SAFETY: removals here are safe by construction — kconfig will not drop a symbol that
# anything we keep `select`s. The residual risk is a board whose DTS needs a driver that
# lived behind a foreign gate; that is what build.sh's assertions and the boot test cover.
# We can only HW-test Pocket S2 + Pocket ACE while the tree carries 15 boards.
#
# TO RE-ENABLE a platform (e.g. a future non-Qualcomm target): delete its line here. Do not
# add a positive `CONFIG_ARCH_x=y` — merge_config would then report a conflict against
# defconfig rather than a clean override.

# ============== Non-Qualcomm arm64 SoC platform gates ==============
# ARCH_QCOM is set in kernel.config and is deliberately absent from this list.

# --- Handheld / mobile / consumer SoC vendors ---
# Apple Silicon SoC family
# CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE is not set
# Samsung Exynos SoC family
# CONFIG_ARCH_EXYNOS is not set
# MediaTek SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_MEDIATEK is not set
# Amlogic Platforms
# CONFIG_ARCH_MESON is not set
# Rockchip Platforms
# CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP is not set
# Allwinner sunxi 64-bit SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI is not set
# NVIDIA Tegra SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_TEGRA is not set
# Spreadtrum SoC platform
# CONFIG_ARCH_SPRD is not set
# HiSilicon SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_HISI is not set
# Realtek Platforms
# CONFIG_ARCH_REALTEK is not set

# --- Embedded / industrial / automotive ---
# NXP i.MX SoC family
# CONFIG_ARCH_MXC is not set
# NXP S32 SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_S32 is not set
# Freescale Layerscape SoC family
# CONFIG_ARCH_LAYERSCAPE is not set
# Texas Instruments K3 multicore SoC architecture
# CONFIG_ARCH_K3 is not set
# Renesas SoC Platforms
# CONFIG_ARCH_RENESAS is not set
# STMicroelectronics STM32 SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_STM32 is not set
# Xilinx ZynqMP Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_ZYNQMP is not set
# Intel SoCFPGA ARMv8 Families
# CONFIG_ARCH_INTEL_SOCFPGA is not set
# Socionext UniPhier SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_UNIPHIER is not set
# Toshiba Visconti SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_VISCONTI is not set
# Tesla platform (Exynos-derived FSD)
# CONFIG_ARCH_TESLA_FSD is not set
# Black Sesame Technologies SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_BST is not set
# Blaize SoC Platforms
# CONFIG_ARCH_BLAIZE is not set
# Intel Keem Bay SoC
# CONFIG_ARCH_KEEMBAY is not set
# Axiado SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_AXIADO is not set
# Axis Communications ARTPEC SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_ARTPEC is not set
# Actions Semi Platforms
# CONFIG_ARCH_ACTIONS is not set
# Airoha SoC Support
# CONFIG_ARCH_AIROHA is not set
# Cixtech SoC family
# CONFIG_ARCH_CIX is not set
# Sophgo SoCs
# CONFIG_ARCH_SOPHGO is not set
# LG Electronics LG1K SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_LG1K is not set

# --- Networking / set-top / broadband silicon ---
# Broadcom BCM2835 family (Raspberry Pi)
# CONFIG_ARCH_BCM2835 is not set
# Broadcom iProc SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_BCM_IPROC is not set
# Broadcom Broadband Carrier Access SoC
# CONFIG_ARCH_BCMBCA is not set
# Broadcom Set-Top-Box SoCs
# CONFIG_ARCH_BRCMSTB is not set
# Marvell EBU SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_MVEBU is not set
# Marvell Berlin SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_BERLIN is not set
# Microchip Sparx5 SoC family
# CONFIG_ARCH_SPARX5 is not set
# Nuvoton MA35 Architecture
# CONFIG_ARCH_MA35 is not set
# Nuvoton NPCM Architecture
# CONFIG_ARCH_NPCM is not set

# --- Server / datacenter arm64 ---
# Cavium Inc. Thunder SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_THUNDER is not set
# Cavium ThunderX2 Server Processors
# CONFIG_ARCH_THUNDER2 is not set
# AppliedMicro X-Gene SOC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_XGENE is not set
# AMD Seattle SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_SEATTLE is not set
# Annapurna Labs Alpine platform
# CONFIG_ARCH_ALPINE is not set
# Socionext SynQuacer SoC Family
# CONFIG_ARCH_SYNQUACER is not set

# --- Reference / emulated boards ---
# We boot real handhelds only; there is no qemu/fastmodel target in this project.
# ARM Ltd Platforms (Versatile Express)
# CONFIG_ARCH_VEXPRESS is not set

# ============== Discrete / add-in GPUs ==============
# Nothing here is reachable on a soldered-Adreno handheld with no add-in card slot.
# NOTE: of the desktop GPU drivers, only nouveau is actually enabled by the arm64 defconfig
# — AMDGPU, RADEON, AST, MGAG200, QXL and VMWGFX are already off, so they are not listed
# here (a `# ... is not set` for an already-unset symbol is noise that reads as protection).
# CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU_BACKLIGHT is not set
